Overall Reflection

This workshop changed my understanding of ethics in ICT because I now see ethical decisions as more than simply choosing what is legal, convenient or technically effective. Kantianism particularly helped me think about whether people are being respected rather than used to achieve an organisation's goals. The other artefacts showed how this idea applies to privacy, ethical hacking, cybersecurity and AI. Together, they demonstrate that ICT professionals have responsibilities to users and society, especially when their decisions can create risks or harm.

